You may do whatever you want with the eWiz source code and other source files
in this repository, which holds the eWiz website and the eWiz update feed (from
here on referred to as the "eWiz Source"), with the following restrictions:

- If you publish any work derived from the eWiz Source, you must make it apparent
  in some way that it is derived from the eWiz Source.

- If you have created an executable program, website or online service (from
  here on called "Your Program") built or compiled from some source code and/or
  other source files (from here on called "Your Source"), and if Your Source
  includes files or source code copied or derived from the eWiz Source, then you
  may only publish Your Program under the following conditions. For a website or
  online service, publishing means making it available to anyone other than
  yourself.

    - Your Program does not contain any malware or hidden malicious content.

    - You may not charge users money for Your Program, and Your Source must
      contain the monetization systems present in the eWiz Source, including the
      license key, checkout and payment systems, without any alterations, and all
      of these systems must be active and working as intended in Your Program,
      paying the original author. That is unless Your Source features substantial
      improvements or additions to the eWiz Source, such that Your Source should
      be considered its own, derivative work, separate from the eWiz Source.

    - You may not publish Your Program under the name "eWiz", or under a name or
      with an icon so similar that users could mistake it for eWiz.

