# Notes on the eWiz License

The eWiz License is modelled on the MMF License that Noah Nuebling wrote for Mac
Mouse Fix, itself based on the MIT and DBAD licenses. It has two goals:

1. To stop people with bad intentions, or people out for a quick buck, from
   publishing sites or apps based on eWiz: a copy of the eWiz website that hands
   out malware in place of the real download, or one that sells eWiz licenses
   while someone other than the author gets paid.

2. To let everyone else do anything they like with the eWiz source code: reuse it
   in their own free or paid projects, write bug fixes and improvements to eWiz and
   publish them, or make a substantial improvement to eWiz and charge for that
   improved version or release it for free.

The license is meant to be open source in spirit, with protections against bad
actors now that eWiz is a paid app. Note that there are no restrictions at all on
how you use the source code, only on publishing programs, websites or services
built from it.

eWiz is "source-available", not open source by the OSI definition, because of the
publishing restrictions above.

Buying eWiz buys a license key for the eWiz app; it does not change these terms,
which govern the source code.

The eWiz app's own repository carries the same license, worded for the Mac app.
Files in this repository that carry their own license notice, such as the
generated Cloudflare type definitions, stay under that notice.
